            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Splendifirous in it's own right, this creamy yet subtle cottage cheese pie has both texture and flavour, as well as a great eye for fashion (haw! haw!). Of course, it should be teamed with blueberries to add a fruity, playful side to the special evening."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sweets4me"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good. I added canned cherries on top after it was done. I also used a graham cracker crust.",
            "datePublished": "2009-02-09T13:25:13.137Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dave"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Are you kidding me? This recipe is absolutely, positively, FANTASTIC!!! When I took it out of the oven and let it cool for about 10 minutes, I tasted it. That's it. It was all over. I sat there by myself and devoured half of the pie. I din't have chopped walnuts in the house, but the almonds worked just fine. Had someone asked me for a taste, I would have told them to take out the baby spoon and that's all you get. I wouldn't rate this recipe a 5 star, but I would rate it a 10 star!!!",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-24T06:23:41.977Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MelissaGG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is excellent! Tastes very similar to cheese cake, but without the heavy weight to each bite, or the calories. I’ve made a number of these using this recipe as the base and blended in different cheesecake recipes (for added flavors) and have loved the results.",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-19T23:24:24.567Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "joysgirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "WOW! I didn't expect to LOVE this pie; I was just trying find a recipe to use a container of cottage cheese before it went bad. This pie is fantastic, brunch/company worthy. I used orange zest instead of lemon and cranberries instead of raisins (my son doesn't like raisins). It turned out beautifully! My picture was an afterthought, since I didn't expect to enjoy it so much.",
            "datePublished": "2023-02-24T20:42:19.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Yoly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I left out the raisins, personal preference and I upped the amount of nuts. I had a very difficult time pressing the cottage cheese through the sieve. I gave up and used it as is. Maybe that was why the pie, though tasty was ‘wet’. If I ever make this again, I will cream the cottage cheese in a food processor or in my vitamix.",
            "datePublished": "2021-08-20T22:40:24.610Z"
          }
        ],
